WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:04.003
Without a hint of irony
or shame,

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:06.139
Senate GOP leader
Mitch McConnell declared

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:09.008
an end to the era of
bipartisanship,

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.210
even as President Biden
continues to entertain

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.612
fruitless talks with
Republicans.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:15.515
Oh, and also a GOP congressman

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:19.018
suggested the Forest Service
should change the course

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:22.655
of the Earth's orbit
to fight climate change.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.957
For more on this,
it's time for A Closer Look.

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:28.261 align:start size:34% position:66% line:0%
♪♪

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.630
One of the many things
the Trump era has revealed

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.031
about our political culture

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:35.134
is that the Republican Party
really has no core ideology

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:37.270
aside from its deep hostility
to democracy.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.572
They have no core
policy positions

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.140
or visions for the future.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.109
And that's why
they don't spend much time

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.144
talking about the things
Joe Biden is actually doing.

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:48.247
Instead, they whine about
Dr. Seuss or Mr. Potato Head

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:51.151
or go on Fox News
and say dumb culture war B.S.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.519
like this from an actual
United States senator

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:54.720
just a few days ago.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.456
-The leadership of the
Democratic Party

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.858
took a hard left
and kept driving.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.993
There are two groups
in charge --

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:03.729
the wokeristas who have contempt
for America

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:07.100
and the managerial elite
who have contempt

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.303
for the American
middle class.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.771
I refer to them
as the, um,

00:01:12.771 --> 00:01:17.243
the vanilla soy, extra-foam
latte crowd.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.145
-Hey, Huckleberry Hound,
you know who's buying

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.514
all the vanilla soy lattes?
It's the middle class.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:22.915
I mean, don't you have
Instagram?

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:25.051
Every third picture
is a smiling soccer parent

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.719
with a seatbelt
over their shoulder,

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:28.087
holding up a Starbucks cup

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.422
with the caption "Live,
laugh, caffeinate."

00:01:30.422 --> 00:01:33.726
Also, a latte with extra foam
is just a cappuccino.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.894
You don't have to be
a coastal elite to know that.

00:01:35.894 --> 00:01:38.064
Just go to Starbucks,
order a latte with extra foam

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.965
and wait for an exasperated
barista to say,

00:01:39.965 --> 00:01:43.503
"So, a cappuccino?"

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:46.105
And let's not forget,
this dude used to be a Democrat

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:49.141
who endorsed John Kerry in 2004
and went to Oxford.

00:01:49.141 --> 00:01:52.212
So I don't quite buy it when he
puts on his fake folksy demeanor

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:54.814
and talks like he's on
Baton Rouge basic cable,

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.415
giving out crawdad
recipes.

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:58.284
[ Imitating Senator Kennedy ]
"Ooh-ee, they extra tasty

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:01.587
if you leave the guts in them."

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:03.690
[ Normally ] I'm willing to bet
that accent isn't even real.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.124
When he's on TV,
he's all like,

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:06.325
[ Imitating Senator Kennedy ]
"Democrats are crazier than

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:09.295
a swamp rat snorting bath salts
in a steamboat."

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:10.796
[ Normally ] But then as soon
as the cameras are off,

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:12.198
he turns to an aide and says,

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.799
[ British accent] "Right, that's
another advert for the telly

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:17.336
done and dusted. Now, switch on
Tottenham versus Man U."

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:19.138
[ Normally ]
The point is, this is all

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:21.774
Republicans have --
this culture war nonsense.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.409
Like when they said
Joe Biden

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.712
wants to ban hamburgers
as part of the Green New Deal.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:28.014
Republicans want you to think
the Green New Deal

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:30.550
is some sort of socialist
plot to destroy America.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.819
Meanwhile, a GOP congressman
suggested during a hearing

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:37.122
this week that a better way
to fight climate change

00:02:37.122 --> 00:02:40.092
would be for the Forest Service
and Bureau of Land Management

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:43.462
to somehow alter the orbit of
the Earth and the moon.

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:47.333
-I understand from what's been
testified to the Forest Service

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.002
and the BLM,

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:53.740
you want very much to work
on the issue of climate change.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:59.078
I was informed
by the past director of NASA

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:02.114
that they have found
that the moon's orbit

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:03.649
is changing slightly

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:07.186
and so is the Earth's orbit
around the sun.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:12.858
We know there's been significant
solar flare activity.

00:03:12.858 --> 00:03:14.827
And so is there anything

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:18.331
that the National Forest Service
or BLM

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:23.970
can do to change the course
of the moon's orbit

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.639
or the Earth's orbit
around the Sun?

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:30.376
Obviously, that would have
profound effects on our climate.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:35.448
-I would have to follow up
with you on that one,

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:36.883
Mr. Gohmert.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.785
-Just to be clear,
that was Congress.

00:03:39.785 --> 00:03:42.087
What you just saw was from,
like, the actual Congress.

00:03:42.087 --> 00:03:44.457
It wasn't a 3:00 a.m.
public access show

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.158
that's supposed to be
about current events,

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:48.761
but the only people who call in
want to talk about UFOs.

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:51.164
"Alright, tonight's topic
is infrastructure.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:52.565
Steve, you're on the line."

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:55.267
"Yeah. I'm curious, do you think
extraterrestrials can drive?

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:57.469
And if so, do you think
that explains the traffic

00:03:57.469 --> 00:04:00.072
on the Verrazzano?
I'll hang up and listen."

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:01.975
Now, there's been
some suggestion

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:03.476
that Gohmert was being sarcastic

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:05.778
as a way to dismiss efforts
to fight climate change,

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.813
which would be just as dumb.

00:04:07.813 --> 00:04:09.815
Either way, these people
would rather change

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:11.217
Earth's actual orbit

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:13.619
than maybe put up some windmills
or drive an electric car.

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:15.588
They literally, literally think

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.289
the world should revolve
around them.

00:04:17.289 --> 00:04:20.726
I also love the long pause
and the promise to follow up,

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:23.429
which she definitely will not,
nor does she have to.

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:26.132
I'm pretty sure Gohmert has the
memory of a golden retriever.

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:28.300
It's not like he's going to roll
into work on Monday and yell,

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.738
"Did the tree lady
call back with the moon answer?"

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:37.910
"I'm having a lousy day
already.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.946
Barista gave me [bleep] for
asking for a latte

00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:43.883
with extra foam."

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.486
Her response was the equivalent
of giving someone at a bar

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:48.754
a fake number
so they'll leave you alone.

00:04:48.754 --> 00:04:50.556
"Yeah, no, I'd love
to go out with you.

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:57.430
Just give me a call at, uh,
1-877-KARS-4-KIDS.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:00.132
I was really hoping to play
the Kars for Kids jingle there,

00:05:00.132 --> 00:05:01.934
but I was told that, much like
"You Can't Touch This"

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.402
by M.C. Hammer,
we can't afford it,

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:06.005
which is why we've been trying
to cut down in the number

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:07.440
of lines we give Wally,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.776
because every time he speaks,
we have to pay him per word.

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:12.878
-But --
-Shut it, Wally.

00:05:12.878 --> 00:05:15.480
Every word you say
is one less word

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:19.385
we could afford
from this genius.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.887
And last time I checked,
well, it's Hammertime,

00:05:21.887 --> 00:05:24.557
not Yammertime.

00:05:27.726 --> 00:05:30.830
There are really times
when you miss the audience.

00:05:36.568 --> 00:05:41.407
What's that?
It would have been the same?

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.242
Also, the best part
about that clip

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:45.745
is there is no way --
no way you could have predicted

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:46.979
where it was going from
where it started.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:48.948
It's like getting cornered
at a cocktail party

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:51.016
by a guy who wants to talk
to you about life insurance

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:52.651
and you think,
"Alright, this is boring."

00:05:52.651 --> 00:05:54.987
So you zone out for 30 seconds
and suddenly you hear

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:57.356
the phrase "zombie
flesh-eating space cicadas."

00:05:57.356 --> 00:06:01.027
Which, side note -- oh, and
can a tangent have a side note?

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:02.594
Can you check with Legal on that
and get back to me?

00:06:02.594 --> 00:06:05.264
Anyway, side note,
as soon as Broadway reopens,

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:07.032
do buy your tickets
for my new musical,

00:06:07.032 --> 00:06:09.234
"Ci-cay-da Ci-cah-da",
starring Christine Baranski,

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:10.702
Harvey Fierstein
and Nathan Lane.

00:06:10.702 --> 00:06:13.605
And we are also thrilled
to announce that Jason Sudeikis

00:06:13.605 --> 00:06:17.810
is joining the cast
as Jason Cicadis.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:20.545
Fresh off his monster success
starring in Ted Grasso.

00:06:20.545 --> 00:06:22.681
[ Crickets chirping ]

00:06:22.681 --> 00:06:25.485
That's not a response.
That's the theme song.

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:29.988
Between "Cicada Cicada"
and "My Zipper",

00:06:29.988 --> 00:06:32.391
plus my new show, "Chicago
Postal Service Police Force",

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:35.461
I will have enough money
to afford an entire line

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:36.562
from "You Can't Touch This".

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:38.697
-Seth --
-Wally!

00:06:38.697 --> 00:06:40.833
M.C. stands
for Master of Ceremonies,

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:43.902
not Master of Cue Cards.

00:06:43.902 --> 00:06:46.005
That's why there's
only the one C.

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:52.811
Every word you say
is one less lyric

00:06:52.811 --> 00:06:55.047
we can afford from this genius.

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:57.216
Anyway, where was I?

00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:59.218
Oh, politics.
Alright.

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:00.987
So that's the Republican Party
we're dealing with,

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:03.689
and Democrats need to be
clear-eyed about that fact.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:06.192
It's a party whose members
believe the Forest Service

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:08.327
has the power
to alter the Earth's orbit,

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:11.630
the wildfires are caused
by secret Jewish space lasers,

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:14.299
and that the election was
hacked by Italian satellites.

00:07:14.299 --> 00:07:15.701
What's their obsession
with space?

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:17.970
Did they all watch the first
episode of "Loki" last night

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.138
and think it was
a documentary?

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:21.107
Side note -- and did legal get
back to us?

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:22.741
So we can --
can't take a side note?

00:07:22.741 --> 00:07:24.177
Let's just do it anyway.

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:27.046
Side note, I'm really hoping
that "Loki" is not a big hit,

00:07:27.046 --> 00:07:28.714
not because I didn't enjoy it,
which I did,

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:31.350
but because I'm really hoping
Owen Wilson's not too tied up

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.951
for the "Wedding Crashers"
sequel that we heard

00:07:32.951 --> 00:07:35.320
"Late Night" are claiming
full credit for.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.789
I mean, if by some chance,
"Loki" takes Wilson away

00:07:37.789 --> 00:07:39.692
from the project,
then, you know,

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:41.093
Vince is going to have to make
a phone call,

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:44.630
and I don't know, I think it
might sound something like this.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:45.964
[ Imitating Vince Vaughn ]
"Buddy, buddy, buddy, you know,

00:07:45.964 --> 00:07:48.633
I love Loki. You know,
he's an imp, he's a trickster.

00:07:48.633 --> 00:07:50.736
His antics are adorable,
but we have to make this movie.

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:52.038
The world is waiting for us."

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:53.305
[ Imitating Owen Wilson ]
"I don't know, man.

00:07:53.305 --> 00:07:56.609
I think Marvel might be
a little more popular."

00:07:56.609 --> 00:07:59.545
Anyway, what was I saying?
Oh, right.

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:02.515
Republicans are too concerned
about culture stuff.

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:05.484
Oh. This is why it's absurd
to contemplate

00:08:05.484 --> 00:08:07.853
bipartisan cooperation
with the Republican Party,

00:08:07.853 --> 00:08:10.423
and yet, for some reason,
Joe Biden and certain members

00:08:10.423 --> 00:08:12.524
of the Democratic Party
like Joe Manchin

00:08:12.524 --> 00:08:14.894
still seem obsessed with it.
This week, for example,

00:08:14.894 --> 00:08:16.995
Biden ended
bipartisan negotiations

00:08:16.995 --> 00:08:20.299
with one group of Republicans
only to start negotiations

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:21.967
with another group
of Republicans.

00:08:21.967 --> 00:08:23.903
-Tonight,
infrastructure negotiations

00:08:23.903 --> 00:08:26.606
entering a new phase,
with President Biden

00:08:26.606 --> 00:08:28.507
ending talks with a group
of Republicans

00:08:28.507 --> 00:08:30.242
led by
Senator Shelley Moore Capito

00:08:30.242 --> 00:08:33.712
on Tuesday and reaching out to
members of a bipartisan group

00:08:33.712 --> 00:08:35.080
of moderate senators.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:36.582
-I'm sorry, which group
of Republicans

00:08:36.582 --> 00:08:38.751
do you think you're going
to find common ground with?

00:08:38.751 --> 00:08:40.720
The group that thinks
the Forest Service has the power

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.788
to alter Earth's orbit
or the group that thinks

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:44.757
the election was hacked
by Italian satellites?

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:47.093
[ Imitating Biden ] "Alright,
folks, how about a compromise?

00:08:47.093 --> 00:08:48.594
How about instead
of the Forest Service,

00:08:48.594 --> 00:08:51.063
we use the Italian satellites
to alter the Earth's orbit?

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:52.297
Do we have a deal?"

00:08:52.297 --> 00:08:55.233
Also, there's a downside
to humoring Republicans,

00:08:55.233 --> 00:08:58.336
and that's time. Every day
wasted on bipartisan talks

00:08:58.336 --> 00:09:00.406
that will inevitably
go nowhere

00:09:00.406 --> 00:09:02.040
is a day that could have
been spent working on

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.709
or passing
much-needed legislation

00:09:03.709 --> 00:09:05.677
on everything from
climate change to voting rights.

00:09:05.677 --> 00:09:08.513
That's Mitch McConnell's goal
to run out the clock.

00:09:08.513 --> 00:09:10.749
Did we learn that lesson
from the Obama era?

00:09:10.749 --> 00:09:12.651
He spent months making
good-faith efforts

00:09:12.651 --> 00:09:13.885
to woo Republicans.

00:09:13.885 --> 00:09:16.389
He went to a House
GOP conference to take questions

00:09:16.389 --> 00:09:18.991
and hosted a summit with them.
In the end, all he got out of it

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:20.759
was zero votes
from Senate Republicans

00:09:20.759 --> 00:09:22.461
for his health care bill
and an annoying,

00:09:22.461 --> 00:09:24.296
pompous lecture
from Paul Ryan.

00:09:24.296 --> 00:09:27.466
-This bill does not
reduce deficits.

00:09:27.466 --> 00:09:30.469
Instead, this bill adds
a new health care entitlement

00:09:30.469 --> 00:09:32.337
at a time
when we have no idea

00:09:32.337 --> 00:09:35.007
how to pay for the entitlements
we already have.

00:09:35.007 --> 00:09:36.208
First, a little bit about CBO.

00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:38.043
I work with them
every single day.

00:09:38.043 --> 00:09:40.579
Very good people,
great professionals.

00:09:40.579 --> 00:09:42.281
They do their jobs well,

00:09:42.281 --> 00:09:45.718
but their job is to score
what is placed in front of them.

00:09:45.718 --> 00:09:47.720
And what has been placed
in front of them

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:49.622
is a bill
that is full of gimmicks

00:09:49.622 --> 00:09:52.591
and smoke and mirrors. And what
do I mean when I say that?

00:09:52.591 --> 00:09:55.327
-Man, look at Obama's face.
That's the moment right then

00:09:55.327 --> 00:09:57.663
when he started thinking
about his Netflix deal.

00:09:57.663 --> 00:09:59.965
[ Imitating Obama ] "Maybe I can
get a part in 'Loki'.

00:09:59.965 --> 00:10:04.637
Uh, Loki! Stop with your antics.
It's time to get serious."

00:10:04.637 --> 00:10:06.472
[ Normally ]
Oh, sir. That's Disney+.

00:10:06.472 --> 00:10:10.475
"But he's Loki. Can't you trick
him into moving to Netflix?"

00:10:10.475 --> 00:10:12.678
See guys, two "Loki" references,
in one Look.

00:10:12.678 --> 00:10:13.879
It was pretty good.

00:10:13.879 --> 00:10:16.648
I wonder if there's
going to be a third one.

00:10:16.648 --> 00:10:17.950
Shoemaker?

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:20.319
Do you think we'll do
rule of threes on "Loki"?

00:10:20.319 --> 00:10:25.524
You're useless. Our material
is getting fresher.

00:10:25.524 --> 00:10:29.695
Next we'll be talking about
cryptocurrencies and Dogecoin,

00:10:29.695 --> 00:10:31.997
or as Sean Hannity
called it last night...

00:10:31.997 --> 00:10:34.266
-OK, you've been
hearing all about it.

00:10:34.266 --> 00:10:39.171
Bitcoin, cryptocurrency.
What is it? Why is it so big?

00:10:39.171 --> 00:10:41.640
What is Bitcoin?
What is block chain?

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:43.041
What is DoggyCoin?

00:10:43.041 --> 00:10:45.578
-Well, apparently you haven't
been hearing all about it.

00:10:45.578 --> 00:10:47.279
"DoggyCoin"
is what my kids call it

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:51.183
when Frisbee leaves a turd
on the carpet.

00:10:51.183 --> 00:10:53.118
Anyway, what were we talking
about? Oh right, the news.

00:10:53.118 --> 00:10:56.421
Senate Republicans couldn't
even produce 10 measly votes

00:10:56.421 --> 00:10:59.525
for a commission to investigate
the January 6th insurrection,

00:10:59.525 --> 00:11:02.228
and this week, they blocked
the Paycheck Fairness Act.

00:11:02.228 --> 00:11:03.896
They're never going to agree
to a deal on,

00:11:03.896 --> 00:11:06.298
say, infrastructure,
especially when their members

00:11:06.298 --> 00:11:08.200
like Tennessee Senator
Marsha Blackburn

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.870
are going on Fox News
and saying stuff like this.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:13.239
-If they want great
infrastructure right now,

00:11:13.239 --> 00:11:16.609
ready-to-build, go build
the wall on the southern border.

00:11:16.609 --> 00:11:18.543
-A wall in the middle
of the desert

00:11:18.543 --> 00:11:20.379
is not infrastructure.
No one can use it,

00:11:20.379 --> 00:11:23.181
drive over it, or through it
unless you paint a tunnel on it,

00:11:23.181 --> 00:11:25.417
and even then, it's only
applicable to roadrunners.

00:11:25.417 --> 00:11:26.785
Also, I thought Trump
already built the wall.

00:11:26.785 --> 00:11:29.054
He kept insisting the wall
was being built. So which is it?

00:11:29.054 --> 00:11:31.757
Did he build it or did he flake
on a core campaign promise?

00:11:31.757 --> 00:11:33.559
Or are you guys calling
for more walls?

00:11:33.559 --> 00:11:35.394
"We need a second wall
to protect the first wall

00:11:35.394 --> 00:11:37.196
because it is flimsy
and shoddily made.

00:11:37.196 --> 00:11:39.198
And the best part is
we don't have to pay for it.

00:11:39.198 --> 00:11:41.166
We can just use..."
-DoggyCoin.

00:11:41.166 --> 00:11:43.502
-The meaningless pursuit
of bipartisanship that will

00:11:43.502 --> 00:11:46.138
never happen is wasting
valuable time and energy

00:11:46.138 --> 00:11:47.740
that could go to far
more productive things.

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:49.809
In fact, McConnell
has already declared

00:11:49.809 --> 00:11:52.444
that his #1 goal
is blocking the Biden agenda.

00:11:52.444 --> 00:11:53.746
And earlier this week,
without even

00:11:53.746 --> 00:11:56.081
a hint of self-awareness,
he said this.

00:11:56.081 --> 00:11:58.016
-As you look to what
the majority leader

00:11:58.016 --> 00:11:59.818
has in mind for June,

00:11:59.818 --> 00:12:03.322
it's pretty clear the era
of bipartisanship is over.

00:12:03.322 --> 00:12:05.357
-Oh, man.
I wonder whose fault that is.

00:12:05.357 --> 00:12:06.925
If this had been the case

00:12:06.925 --> 00:12:08.561
the Mare of Easttown
was investigating,

00:12:08.561 --> 00:12:10.195
she would have solved it
in the first five minutes

00:12:10.195 --> 00:12:12.431
and spent the next six episodes
trying to figure out

00:12:12.431 --> 00:12:15.467
why all the kids in town
looked like they came from L.A..

00:12:15.467 --> 00:12:17.970
"I don't know, Mare.
Their teeth are real good."

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:20.272
Republicans have no interest
in making government work,

00:12:20.272 --> 00:12:21.540
only in controlling it.

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:23.942
That's why they're laser-focused
on subverting democracy,

00:12:23.942 --> 00:12:26.511
spreading the big lie that
the 2020 election was stolen,

00:12:26.511 --> 00:12:29.148
posing for photos at the
Minnesota violent insurrection

00:12:29.148 --> 00:12:32.150
to overturn the results, and
passing voter suppression laws

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:33.419
so they can never lose again.

00:12:33.419 --> 00:12:36.087
They think they're beyond
democratic accountability,

00:12:36.087 --> 00:12:37.555
no matter how unpopular
they are.

00:12:37.555 --> 00:12:39.725
Basically,
when it comes to voters,

00:12:39.725 --> 00:12:41.994
their attitude,
much like M.C. Hammer, is --

00:12:41.994 --> 00:12:44.897
-You can't.

00:12:44.897 --> 00:12:46.565
-This is on you, Wally.

00:12:46.565 --> 00:12:48.968
-I'm sorry, Seth. I try to stop,
but I just can't.

00:12:48.968 --> 00:12:49.835
-Why?

00:12:49.835 --> 00:12:52.170
-Because I'm "2 Legit 2 Quit".

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.271
[ Crickets chirping ]

00:12:53.271 --> 00:12:56.175
[ Laughs ]

00:12:58.677 --> 00:13:00.946
-Good one.
-Yeah.

00:13:00.946 --> 00:13:02.381
I felt pretty good about it.

00:13:04.616 --> 00:13:05.817
Anyway, what was I doing?

00:13:05.817 --> 00:13:06.985
Oh, right, I was trying
to end the segment.

00:13:06.985 --> 00:13:09.087
Basically, when it comes
to bipartisanship,

00:13:09.087 --> 00:13:10.389
